   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nVal</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI think we have previously had requests for code to produce what you want. I ask that you read through this thread from the list, going back a couple of years.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/rAIJy5fhslI/m/vjzlA9a0BgAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/rAIJy5fhslI/m/vjzlA9a0BgAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471471415000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nVm7gW4e9TXF1OcrHR_iP\">https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/rAIJy5fhslI/m/vjzlA9a0BgAJ</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nfocus on the exchanges in the thread in May 2023 and January 2024</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI revised the attached R code about 18 months ago to cope with both half normal and hazard rate key functions. I&#39;m making the assumption that you are conversant in R. The code is not brilliantly documented, but in essence it should extract the covariate coefficients\r\n from a fitted model object and produce what you want.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Val Harvey &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">val_h...@hotmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 24 October 2025 14:56<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] Average probability of detection values</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-width:0px;border-style:solid;margin:0.5rem 0px;font-family:fkGroteskNeue,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Hiragino Sans&quot;,&quot;PingFang SC&quot;,&quot;Apple SD Gothic Neo&quot;,&quot;Yu Gothic&quot;,&quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;,&quot;Microsoft JhengHei&quot;,Meiryo;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.08px;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\nBonjour,</p>\r\n<p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-width:0px;border-style:solid;margin:1rem 0px 0.5rem;font-family:fkGroteskNeue,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Hiragino Sans&quot;,&quot;PingFang SC&quot;,&quot;Apple SD Gothic Neo&quot;,&quot;Yu Gothic&quot;,&quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;,&quot;Microsoft JhengHei&quot;,Meiryo;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.08px;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\nIs it possible to retrieve the values of the average prediction curve for a given model — specifically, the curve shown as a solid line in this figure? Are these values saved within the object and available for later retrieval? I would like to calculate the\r\n average detection probability of my model at different distances.</p>\r\n<p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-width:0px;border-style:solid;margin:1rem 0px 0.5rem;font-family:fkGroteskNeue,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Hiragino Sans&quot;,&quot;PingFang SC&quot;,&quot;Apple SD Gothic Neo&quot;,&quot;Yu Gothic&quot;,&quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;,&quot;Microsoft JhengHei&quot;,Meiryo;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.08px;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\nOtherwise, for models that contain only categorical variables, I’ve been able to recreate the curves and obtain the average curve values. However, I don’t fully understand how to reproduce this information for models that include both categorical and continuous\r\n variables.</p>\r\n<p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-width:0px;border-style:solid;margin:1rem 0px 0.5rem;font-family:fkGroteskNeue,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Hiragino Sans&quot;,&quot;PingFang SC&quot;,&quot;Apple SD Gothic Neo&quot;,&quot;Yu Gothic&quot;,&quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;,&quot;Microsoft JhengHei&quot;,Meiryo;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.08px;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\nThank you in advance for your help with this question,</p>\r\n<img src=\"https://ci4.googleusercontent.com/proxy/8VzuFy_Mmx57837HSDjQOgf8nC04wOsbpvJYV66pxrui7Li2Aoh6_QdMAIjh6IWKmFMX_rUWTw27zG5vt_vF1BaapPmVkmEhpPi9bb_ZBObd4zvUpFmxmLSSXA=s0-d-e1-ft#http://127.0.0.1:11915/graphics/eba4ec7e-2ea4-41da-acc1-722641e7a999.png\">\r\n<br>\r\n<p></p></div></div>"
